+# Receiving worker execution
+
+Sections labeled as complete role, instruction, or skill bodies contain the supplied files' full instruction content. Apply them directly, including nested requests to read the same file, without reopening those files. This also applies to complete instruction bodies already in your context. A path, summary, excerpt, or truncated body does not replace the full file. Read required bodies that are absent or incomplete, including linked references and applied principle leaves. Delivery alone does not show that an instruction was followed.
+
+The receiving executor declared above is the harness running this worker. Supplied pstack files and preference helpers belong to the launching host. Keep their workflow, original role instructions, ordered seats, saved model choices, and configuration authority. Their host-specific tool names describe that launching host.
+
+For a resolved entry whose executor matches this receiving harness, delegate with the native subagent tools actually exposed here. Pass the selected exact model, supported effort, and complete role and template brief. For a read-only workflow such as How, use the native read-only kind where available, or a native general-purpose seat with an explicit no-edits brief when it preserves the requested settings. A host-specific `agentType` applies only in its own host. Parent aliases refer to the actual native parent in this receiving runtime, without acquiring a foreign executor from launching-host metadata.
+
+The launching parent's external-run background recipe starts this worker. Native delegation inside this worker retains upstream's asynchronous launch, steer, and resume behavior through this harness's own completion mechanism. For native Claude `Agent` or `Task` calls, set `run_in_background: true` when the exposed schema supports that field. Native Codex delegation already uses asynchronous handles; use its actual schema without adding a background field. Launch independent seats before waiting and collect their completed results. Native delegation does not require re-entering the external runner or creating an external-run receipt for a native child. Preserve the current task scope and read-only or write permissions.
+
+On macOS, a Codex receiving executor's default workspace sandbox blocks Chromium-based browsers, local listening ports, Git metadata writes, and network access. Run those task-authorized commands with escalated sandbox permissions on the first attempt. The configured reviewer decides whether they run.
+
+Exact selections for another executor keep their chosen route. If the available controls cannot express a required executor, model, effort, or worker role, report the exact capability gap. Preserve the workflow's existing fallback and diversity rules without inventing a substitute or expanding permissions.
+
+A Pi receiving executor has no established native nested delegation. Its explicitly selected built-in tools do not inherit the parent's MCP, full conversation, permissions, or OS read-only enforcement. Keep the launching host's saved provider, model, effort, role shape, fresh-worker rules, and required diversity gates. Report a missing required capability instead of inventing native tools or a parent launch route.
